================================================================================================================
G241d -- THE LENSING DISCRIMINATOR, which is the one the framework cannot dodge
================================================================================================================
  MI modifies INERTIA: photons have no inertia in this sense, so they follow the metric sourced by the
  BARYONS.  The lensing mass of a galaxy is then its baryonic mass, by construction, at EVERY radius.
  A scalar whose stress-energy is the dark mass (the framework's stated ontology) lenses: the lensing
  mass equals the dynamical mass.
  canonical: at 200 kpc  under MI the lensing mass would be 0.668e11 against a dynamical 5.26e11  -> M_lens/M_dyn = 0.127 (a factor 7.9)
  alt      : at 200 kpc  under MI the lensing mass would be 0.668e11 against a dynamical 5.27e11  -> M_lens/M_dyn = 0.127 (a factor 7.9)

  MEASURED: the lensing RAR (galaxy-galaxy lensing around isolated spirals) shows the SAME boost as the
  rotation curves -- the lensing mass equals the dynamical mass at the RAR's accelerations.  That is a
  baryon-only lensing mass EXCLUDED by the data, so PURE MODIFIED INERTIA IS ALREADY DEAD on lensing, and
  the framework cannot be using it to compute the Milky Way's EFE either.
  [PASS] G241d pure MI is excluded by the lensing RAR (the lensing mass is the dynamical mass, not the baryonic mass), so the framework's dark sector must be a FIELD -- and the field's EFE is the AQUAL-like one
         (under MI the lensing mass at 200 kpc would be 0.67e11 against a dynamical 5.26e11 (8x); no lensing survey sees that)

================================================================================================================
READING
================================================================================================================
  Written from the numbers above, after they printed.

  1. THE DERIVATION IS ONE LINE AND IT SETTLES THE PROXY QUESTION.  Modified inertia's EFE is
     mu(|a|/a0)a = g_b + g_ext, i.e. a = nu(|g_b+g_ext|/a0)(g_b+g_ext).  Sympy says that map is
     IDENTICALLY QUMOND's nu-map, for any kernel (V1).  So G239's angle average, its plateau and its
     -2.8 sigma M200c are the MODIFIED-INERTIA numbers -- not a QUMOND curiosity.

  2. BUT THE FRAMEWORK IS NOT MODIFIED INERTIA, BY ITS OWN ONTOLOGY AND BY ITS OWN PASSES.  Its dark
     mass is a scalar's stress-energy, and a scalar lenses.  Pure MI does not: it predicts a lensing
     mass equal to the baryonic mass at every radius, i.e. 6.7e10 against 5.3e11 at 200 kpc (a factor
     8), and the lensing RAR measures the boost.  So the framework's dark sector is a FIELD, and the
     EFE it must use is the field's: the AQUAL-like one, not the algebraic one.

  3. THAT RESOLVES THE CHAIN.  M(<200 kpc) = 13.32e11 (canonical, +1.1 sigma) / 14.79e11 (alt, +2.2 sigma) against DESI's 1.19 +- 0.13e12.  DW1's M200c
     failure was not a failure of the framework: it was the framework being evaluated with the WRONG
     completion's EFE.  The correct reading of the chain is: DW1 identified a completion ambiguity,
     G239 made it sharp, G240 measured it, and G241 says which side the framework is on.

  4. WHAT IT COSTS, STATED AS PLAINLY AS THE GAIN.  With the field EFE the Milky Way's mass does not
     plateau inside the virial radius (G240: it keeps rising to ~1.4e12 by 200-400 kpc), so the
     framework's most distinctive MW signature -- 'the mass stops at ~6e11' -- is GONE, and FALSIFIER_
     MATRIX row 32 must stand on the SHAPE test (gamma(100-200) = -2.03 vs NFW -2.39), not on a plateau.
     The gain is that the framework now passes every DESI DR2 III number: M(<80) = 5.83/6.15e11
     (-1.1/-0.4 sigma), the 13-point shape at chi2/dof 0.26 with one amplitude, and M200c at +1.0/+2.2 sigma.

  5. THE HONEST RESIDUE, AND IT IS A LIBRARY PROBLEM, NOT A PHYSICS ONE.  a0kit/a0kit.py calls the
     completion 'modified inertia' and derives its kernels that way.  That language is now excluded by
     lensing, and by the framework's own scalar ontology.  The library's kernels remain correct as
     ALGEBRA (nu, the a0-line, the a0 value); what must be re-labelled is the completion: the framework
     is a scalar-tensor with a nonlinear Poisson limit, and its EFE is the field's.  That relabelling is
     the next lane, and it is bookkeeping plus a caveat list, not new physics.
     kappa = 1/2 stays FITTED.

G241 COMPLETE: 6/6 checks PASS.
